{"posts":[{"id":"dbrrbd_p54_1326","t":"HI IT'S ME AGAIN WITH A FEW MORE HOME WORKS\n\nI'M THINKING MORE ABOUT THE ZONE, ESPECIALLY FRESH ZONES\n\nI'M TRYING TO UNDERSTAND THEM BETTER","a":"omidfxt","d":"","n":"#1326","p":54,"im":["0dbd4ebd1397209a92e0b6ad6c98d8b2430d9ba5","1f4be176a392973c5d3cc90812e9f3f2f6513852","d8aa0705de8a38f9a50b094589ab09ff967f9ef1"],"m":1326},{"id":"dbrrbd_p54_1327","t":"Hi All...\n\nI just came across this site and would like to participate / contribute with the aim of meeting other traders and improving my own reading of the market.\n\nHere's my 1st post on GBPUSD;\n\nAnalysis of the Daily & 5min charts from Thurs and Fri 24th / 25th March.\n\nHigher Time Frame Daily - Chart shows 4 down days followed by Thursday color change candle, up day followed by Friday down again-down Lower Time Frame 5min - Chart shows Thursday color change candle, up day followed by Friday down again-up Thurs was a rally up 130 pips Fri was a 40pip consolidation day\n\nAssuming we followed the short term trend (Thurs up move) and took only buy trades there were at least 4 x 20pip trades giving 80pips potential during the London session (entries at 8am, 11am, 12.30pm and 14.30pm)... and that's ignoring the 2 possible entries during the Asian session (at 2.30am and 5.00am).\n\nAbove 6 possible trades appear to be counter to the long term trend.\n\nKey Levels for Next Week 28th to 1st\n\nHigher Time Frame Daily - It may continue downward to 1.4040 or 1.4000 Lower Time Frame 5min - 1.4080 looks like a potential target\n\nI'd appreciate any comments...","a":"pipcapital","d":"","n":"#1327","p":54,"im":["ffe197532831968f7236b47e64bebe9ad60ffe5e","e8bccb58f9172cebd66f471662d89d062ad9219c"],"m":1327},{"id":"dbrrbd_p54_1328","t":"Hi RTMs A few more home works\n\ni think as long as i'm doing my home works, i'm getting better and can feel the chart more easily i'll be glad to read your comments","a":"omidfxt","d":"","n":"#1328","p":54,"im":["d86603890975045aea36309dc98594333b